From: xtandard-image
Subject: [PATCH] A caption must be a byte array

Found by fuzzing (Go FuzzJXR, confirmed with ASan): ParsePFDEntry
terminated a caption tag of any type as a UTF-16 string, so a SHORT or
LONG caption wrote through its number as if it were a pointer. Only a
byte array is kept.
---
--- a/jxrgluelib/JXRGlueJxr.c
+++ b/jxrgluelib/JXRGlueJxr.c
@@ -1730,6 +1730,13 @@
                 pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption.VT.pbVal);
             assert(0 == pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption.VT.pwszVal[uCount/sizeof(U16) - 1]); // Confirm null-term
             //  make sure null term (ReadPropvar allocated enough space for this)
+            // Only a byte array is a caption: any other tag type stored a
+            // number where the pointer would be (asserts are compiled out).
+            if ((DPKVT_BYREF | DPKVT_UI1) != pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption.vt ||
+                NULL == pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption.VT.pbVal) {
+                memset(&pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption, 0, sizeof(pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption));
+                break;
+            }
             pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption.VT.pwszVal[uCount/sizeof(U16)] = 0;
             pID->WMP.sDescMetadata.pvarCaption.vt = DPKVT_LPWSTR;
             break;
